.el .ds Aq '
.TH mnnn-pipe 1  "mnnn-pipe 2.16.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-pipe \- Pipe data through code spaces: a source (a live search of any kind, a journal, a model query or a code space\*(Aqs output), then steps (code spaces, or live searches that filter), then optionally a target that keeps the result (a journal or a model)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn pipe\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-to\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-\-rows\fR] [\fB\-\-chunk\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-keep\-header\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISOURCE\fR> [\fISTEPS\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Pipe data through code spaces: a source (a live search of any kind, a journal, a model query or a code space\*(Aqs output), then steps (code spaces, or live searches that filter), then optionally a target that keeps the result (a journal or a model)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fI<TO>\fR
Save the final output too (any save above; repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the output frame as JSON
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-rows\fR \fI<ROWS>\fR [default: 30]
Table rows to print (0: all)
.TP
\fB\-\-chunk\fR \fI<CHUNK>\fR [default: 0]
With `\-` (standard input) as the source: run the pipe on every N lines as they arrive, so an open TUI sees it progress. 0: all at once
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
With `\-`: parse standard input with a built\-in parser code space first (csv, json, ndjson), shown as the pipe\*(Aqs first step. Without it the data arrives raw (a `text` column) for your own parser step
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\-header\fR
With \-\-chunk: repeat the first line (a header) at the top of every chunk (implied by \-\-format csv)
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISOURCE\fR>
Where the data comes from: search:NAME, journal:NAME, code:SPACE, model:QUERY (or a bare model query), or `\-` for standard input (raw text: add a parser step, or \-\-format)
.TP
[\fISTEPS\fR]
Steps in order: code:SPACE (or a space name), search:NAME (keeps the rows it matches), or a save that passes the data on unchanged, like `tee`: journal:NAME (a new entry with the data), model:NAME (new records), project:NAME[/J], org:ORG[/J] or net[:EXCHANGE|all][/J] (a journal entry kept in the project, given to the org, shared on the network). Save at any step
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v2.16.0
.SH SEE ALSO
